es from the backend. The actor serializes incoming messages and commands but runs completion processing only on tick branches.'\nm['core_overview']['context']['source_ids'] += [load,init,ble,loop]\nm['core_overview']['connection']['explanation'] += ' Client assignment records survive incoming higher-ballot synchronization until a later notifier drain. Whether the assigned entry survives depends on adopted history, rather than on numeric decided-index advancement alone.'\nm['core_overview']['connection']['source_ids'] += [notify,assign,loop]\nm['core_overview']['open_details'] += ['Persistent backend failure/crash durability.','Actor assignment consumption after unchosen history is superseded.','Actor event backpressure and compacted subscription cursor handling.']\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='ActorState::drain_notifiers',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-runtime-notify'],reason='Does numeric decided-index success precede recognition that a different entry replaced this pending operation under a new ballot?',source_ids=[notify,api,err,'src-sync'],high_consequence=True))\n# Reverse indexes belong to the controller.\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n f.pop('established_by',None);f.pop('consumed_by',None)\njson.dump(m,open('core-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='Can append_notify report success for an assigned but unchosen entry after a higher-ballot leader replaces that entry and decides the same index before the origin actor next drains notifiers?',importance='False success would let a caller treat an absent write as committed even if consensus itself chooses a consistent different value.',source_ids=[api,err,notify,assign,loop,'src-leader','src-sync'],participants=['Origin actor and old leader','New leader','Quorum peers'],objects=['Pending operation EntryId','Assignment index and ballot','Decided log entry'],contexts=['Three-node fixed configuration','Non-compacted log with reliable storage','Higher ballot while client operation remains pending'],event_paths=['append_notify -> append_tracked -> record_assignment','higher ballot Prepare/Promise quorum -> sync_log -> AcceptSync','handle_incoming_tracked -> later tick -> drain_notifiers'],activity_classes=['A7','A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['b-runtime-assign','b-runtime-notify'],fact_ids=['f-runtime-assignment'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b-formation':'Quorum chooses replacement history and advances its decided prefix.','b-prepare':'Establishes newer ballot and invalidates old authority.','b-follow':'Applies higher-ballot synchronized history at origin.','b-storage':'Stores the synchronized replacement and decision metadata.','b-read':'Observes actual decided content independently of completion result.','b-runtime-loop':'Allows incoming protocol work between notifier drains.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Superseded rejects old assignments if index is not yet decided.','Quorum adoption preserves entries represented in selected prior history; a ballot change alone is insufficient.','Deferred batch assignments have an additional ballot check.'],unknowns=['Need actual legal history proving original entry never reached the quorum selecting replacement, origin applied replacement, and pending future had not already resolved Superseded.'],trigger_rationale='Direct interface promise and success-before-supersession branch give a precise operation-correspondence discriminator. A legal three-node history can test it without duplicate or reordered same-link delivery assumptions; this is stronger grounded than the unresolved same-ballot transport or heartbeat-duplication questions.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',priority=3)\nclaim=dict(id='claim-notify-correspondence',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='If append_notify for an entry returns Ok(k), the decided log entry denoted by k must be that submitted entry; decision of a different 